  "design": {
    "decision": "Cash [♦] honors by leading them early, before opponents void the suit, instead of holding them back to cover or to win the last trick; also favours buying [♦] honors over [♦] length.",
    "opponent": "Revealed on the first [♦] honor lead. Opponents can duck the [A♦] lead and save their own [♦] honors, or void [♦] so later honor leads get trumped.",
    "rationale": "This is the honors line's lead piece. The GDD's honors line 'owns the A, K and Q and cashes them early', and this sigil pays exactly for that act. It pairs with the kept honor-win points without duplicating them, because leading a [♦] honor pays even when the trick is trumped. It uses the standard honors range [J] through [A]. The suit-plus-range filter costs simplicity (C 6), which I accept because the honors line has no lead payoff.",
